    "title": "File-write tool writing a code-execution sink (GTFOBin)",
    "desc": "A file-write utility (dd, tee, cp, install) wrote - or any process's file access touched - a sink that grants code execution or persistence: the dynamic-loader preload list (/etc/ld.so.preload, /etc/ld.so.conf.d/), a login profile script (/etc/profile.d/, /etc/profile, /etc/bash.bashrc, /etc/environment), or an rc/init drop-in. Writing arbitrary content into one of these through a trusted tool is the GTFOBins file-write abuse (MITRE T1565.001 Stored Data Manipulation), and the sink itself is the persistence/escalation payload - a preloaded library runs in every dynamically linked process (T1574.006), a profile script runs for every login shell (T1546.004). sudoers, cron, PAM and authorized_keys have their own dedicated rules; this adds the loader/profile sinks that were a gap.",
